WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.270
In arithmetic, 3 plus 4 is 7.

2
00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:04.410
Always.

3
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:07.880
Now push a box with two
forces of 5 newtons.

4
00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:10.450
Both the same way: 10 newtons.

5
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.010
Opposite ways: 0 newtons.

6
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.470
The two forces cancel completely.

7
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.860
Same sizes, different answers.

8
00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.600
Direction matters.

9
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:23.550
So when does 3 plus 4 make exactly 5?

10
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.530
In this mission, you'll sort
quantities into scalars,

11
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.780
with size only, and vectors,
with size and direction.

12
00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:35.000
Then you'll add vectors along a line,
where a minus sign means a direction,

13
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.760
not a smaller size.

14
00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:41.400
Your mission: find out when
3 plus 4 really does make 5.
